    "title": "2026 Oscars live stream, start time, TV channel for Academy Awards",
    "text": "The stars are out in Hollywood for one of the greatest nights in entertainment on Sunday, March 15, with the 2026 Oscars set to take place at the Dolby Theatre in Los Angeles, California. Late-night talk show host Conan O’Brien is hosting the 98th annual Academy Awards, which will honor the standouts in film from the past year. MORE: 2026 Oscars Governors Ball menu by Wolfgang Puck revealed Ryan Coogler’s Sinners leads the way with 16 nominations, setting a record for the most in Oscar history, followed by Paul Thomas Anderson’s One Battle After Another with 13. A full list of nominees can be seen here. Ryan Coogler, left, Danai Gurira and Michael B. Jordan arrive at Variety’s Creative Impact Awards and 10 Directors to Watch during the Palm Springs International Film Festival at the Parker Palm Springs on Friday, January 4, 2019. Psiffcreativeimpactawards5060 It’s going to be interesting to see whether Michael B. Jordan, who took home the SAG Award for Best Actor, can continue to bring home the hardware or whether Timothee Chalamet will bounce back for the win after some negative press in recent weeks. The awards ceremony is set to begin at 7:00 p.m. ET on ABC. All of the information you need to watch the Oscars award ceremony can be seen below. — Watch the Oscars Red Carpet Show live on Fubo (free trial) — 2026 Oscars TV & viewing info Mar 27, 2022; Los Angeles, CA, USA; Oscar trophies are prepared backstage during the 94th Academy Awards at the Dolby Theatre. Mandatory Credit: Al Seib/A.M.P.A.S/Handout via USA TODAY NETWORK Date: Sunday, March 15, 2026Start Time: 7:00 p.m. ETLocation: Hollywood, Los Angeles, CaliforniaVenue: Dolby TheatreTV Info: ABCLive Stream: Stream 1 Your best bet for watching the Red Carpet Show via streaming is through Fubo TV. Fubo includes a lineup of the top sports networks like ESPN, FS1, CBS Sports Network & more, along with networks like ABC, CBS, and NBC to get big headlines and expert analysis from TV’s most popular shows and events. — Enjoy free coverage of the top news & trending stories on The Big Lead — NFL: Updated 2026 NFL salary cap space for all 32 teams after first free agency wave MARCH MADNESS: Dick Vitale selects ‘All Rolls Royce PTPERS’ for 2025-26 college basketball season OSCARS: Full list of nominees for the 98th Academy Awards WORLD BASEBALL CLASSIC: USA-Dominican Republic, WBC semifinals pitching matchup confirmed GOLF: 2026 Players Championship payouts for full $25M pursue VIRAL: Miami Open introduces Love All Frosé cocktail in eye-catching cup",
